.TH zcalc "" "Command"
.SH NAME
zcalc \- GUI calculator
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBzcalc [\fIoptions\fB]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
zcalc -- GUI calculator
Usage:	zcalc [ options ]
Keys:	digits . + - * / ^ = c=clear e=CE n=+/- p=pi BS=rubout
	s=sin o=cos t=tan l=ln g=log j=e^x r=sqrt i=1/x
.HE
.B zcalc
is the calculator of the
.SM COHERENT
GUI.
It must be run under the
.B zview
desktop.
It shows a display over a fixed grid of buttons; every button also
has a key equivalent, so the calculator can be driven entirely from
the keyboard.
Arithmetic is double precision; the trigonometric functions work in
radians.
It accepts the standard window
.I options
of GUI applications; see
.BR zview .
.PP
The accepted keys:
.DS
.ta 6n 20n
	\fB0-9, .\fR	enter a number
	\fB+ \- /\fR	add, subtract, divide
	\fB*, x\fR	multiply
	\fB^\fR	y to the power x
	\fB=, RETURN\fR	equals
	\fBc\fR	Clear: start over (also clears Error)
	\fBe\fR	CE: clear the entry, keep the pending operation
	\fBn\fR	change the sign of the display
	\fBp\fR	enter pi
	\fBBS, DEL\fR	rub out the last typed digit
	\fBs o t\fR	sin, cos, tan
	\fBl g\fR	ln, log10
	\fBj\fR	e to the power x
	\fBr\fR	square root
	\fBi\fR	1/x
.DE
The letter commands are lower-case; only
.BR c ,
.BR e ,
.BR n ,
.B p
and
.B x
also work in upper case.
The pending operator is shown at the left edge of the display.
Operators are applied immediately, left to right; there is no
precedence and no parentheses.
.PP
Division by zero, overflow past 1e99, and a function applied outside
its domain show
.BR Error ,
which locks the calculator until
.BR c .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR zview ,
.BR bc ,
.B dc
.SH NOTES
The window has a fixed size (the
.B \-S
option is ignored) and there is no quit key; close the window from
its menu.
A typed entry holds at most 13 characters, and results are shown to
at most 10 significant digits.
